The E-01 capture contradicts the claim that no page describes a budget. Line 60 of research/raw/2026-10-12-github-orchestratorinc-agent-orchestrato-github-03a93e25.md holds the text of a commit, "feat(cloud): Stripe billing with plan slots, usage limits and resets". It describes:
- "one reserved orchestrator slot, the remaining slots for workers (including sessions an orchestrator spawns)";
- usage checked against "the rolling window and the weekly limit", kept as "a ledger of running session-minutes, sampled each minute";
- "Waking a paused session ... is refused when over the plan";
- an enforcer that "pauses running sessions of over-limit organizations between turns, never mid-turn".
This is a budget mechanism that is enforced, not just displayed. It is Cloud-only, it comes from commit text rather than docs, and its code lives in `cloud/`, the folder K-1 says was not read. K-2's day-one step searches only `backend/internal/`, so it would miss it.
